+// Order of the zero_point addition relative to the rounding step. The
+// documented definition is qx = clamp(zero_point + round(x / scale)); ATen's
+// own ARM kernels follow it (see quantize_val_arm below: it rounds first and
+// adds zero_point to the *integer* result), and so do fbgemm's AVX2
+// specializations that serve the x86 build. fbgemm's generic instantiation --
+// the one an aarch64 build selects -- defaults to LEGACY=true, i.e.
+// nearbyint(zero_point + x / scale), which differs in exactly-halfway cases
+// (x = -4.5, zero_point = 5: rounding 0.5 ties-to-even yields 0 instead of 1).
+// Select the documented order on ARM so quantize_val, quantize_vec and the
+// quantize_per_tensor kernel all agree there; other targets keep fbgemm's
+// default so nothing changes for x86.
+#if defined(__ARM_NEON__) || defined(__aarch64__)
+constexpr bool quantize_legacy_order_arm = false;
+#else
+constexpr bool quantize_legacy_order_arm = true;
+#endif
